<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    The Mine designation (RimWorld: Core/Defs/DesignationDefs, DesignationDefOf.Mine) - "dig this cell out",
    the mark AI.WorkGiver_Miner reads and the only thing that makes a citizen pick up a pick.

    targetType Cell: the mark sits on the ground, not on the rock, so it is read by cell (the miner asks
    "is this cell marked") and survives nothing but the rock being mined out.

    removeIfBuildingDespawned is the whole of how a Mine mark ends. RimWorld's Building.DeSpawn calls
    DesignationManager.Notify_BuildingDespawned, which removes every mark in the footprint whose def sets this;
    Things/Mineable.DeSpawn does the same here. RimWorld's own XML for this def is not in the code-only
    decompile this port is checked against, so the flag is set from the mechanism rather than from a file:
    without it nothing ever ends a Mine mark, because mined-out rock is the only event that should.

    designateCancelable stays at its default (true): a player may always withdraw a mine mark.
  -->

  <DesignationDef>
    <defName>Mine</defName>
    <label>mine</label>
    <targetType>Cell</targetType>
    <removeIfBuildingDespawned>true</removeIfBuildingDespawned>
  </DesignationDef>

</Defs>
